    "summary": "<p>Eight fused, level-shifted outputs. Up to 4,096 pixels at 40 fps from Art-Net, sACN or DDP. Flash it from the browser, find it with PixelPilot.</p>",
    "description": "<p>The board most people start with. Eight outputs cover a 16 × 16 matrix wall or a large lithophane lamp array.</p><p>Every output is fused at 5 A and level-shifted to 5 V. Power comes in on a screw terminal at anything from 5 to 24 V, and the USB-C port doubles as a console and a flashing port.</p>",
